1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,961
Orchard Core builds pages from shapes, and creating a shape takes code that

2
00:00:05,961 --> 00:00:07,859
reads properties by name.

3
00:00:07,859 --> 00:00:15,392
The OrchardCore.SourceGenerators project writes that code when you build, and warns about shape and feature mistakes.

4
00:00:15,392 --> 00:00:19,740
In this video, we'll go through each generator and each analyzer.

5
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:26,497
A shape holds the data to display.

6
00:00:26,497 --> 00:00:30,918
Without generated code, Orchard Core fills a shape from an object by reading

7
00:00:30,918 --> 00:00:35,662
its properties through reflection, and creates a strongly typed shape from a proxy

8
00:00:35,662 --> 00:00:38,520
class that derives from your model, at runtime.

9
00:00:39,270 --> 00:00:43,703
The OrchardCore.SourceGenerators project moves that work to build time.

10
00:00:43,703 --> 00:00:49,056
Its generators write the code for argument classes, anonymous objects and typed shapes,

11
00:00:49,056 --> 00:00:52,280
and its analyzers report warnings while you build.

12
00:00:56,480 --> 00:00:59,465
Start with a class that holds the arguments.

13
00:00:59,465 --> 00:01:05,673
Mark it with GenerateArguments, and declare it partial, because the generator adds the other half.

14
00:01:05,673 --> 00:01:10,210
This is NavigationArguments, from the menu filter of the Admin module.

15
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:14,904
The generated half derives from PropertyBasedNamedEnumerable.

16
00:01:14,904 --> 00:01:19,553
It keeps the property names in an array, reports their count, and returns

17
00:01:19,553 --> 00:01:23,497
each value from a switch on the index, so the class reads its

18
00:01:23,497 --> 00:01:26,440
own properties directly, without reflection.

19
00:01:27,190 --> 00:01:32,379
Pass an instance to Arguments.From, and it returns the instance itself, because the

20
00:01:32,379 --> 00:01:34,827
class already provides named values.

21
00:01:34,827 --> 00:01:39,433
The menu filter creates the Navigation shape this way, with the menu name

22
00:01:39,433 --> 00:01:40,890
and the route data.

23
00:01:41,640 --> 00:01:44,211
Four rules follow from the generated code.

24
00:01:44,211 --> 00:01:48,711
The class is partial, its public instance properties with a getter are listed,

25
00:01:48,711 --> 00:01:52,943
properties inherited from a base class are left out, and the class cannot

26
00:01:52,943 --> 00:01:54,550
name another base class.

27
00:01:58,750 --> 00:02:03,166
An anonymous object has no name to mark, so another generator uses an

28
00:02:03,166 --> 00:02:06,641
interceptor, a generated method that replaces a call.

29
00:02:06,641 --> 00:02:11,940
This method from the navigation code passes one to Arguments.From, and the generator

30
00:02:11,940 --> 00:02:14,060
finds that call at build time.

31
00:02:14,810 --> 00:02:17,570
The generated method replaces that call.

32
00:02:17,570 --> 00:02:22,430
It casts the object back to its anonymous type through type inference, then

33
00:02:22,430 --> 00:02:27,770
reads each property directly and passes the values and the names to Arguments.From.

34
00:02:28,520 --> 00:02:33,839
An object without generated code takes the reflection path, which caches the property

35
00:02:33,839 --> 00:02:35,418
lookup for each type.

36
00:02:35,418 --> 00:02:40,328
The interceptor skips an anonymous object that has no public property, and one

37
00:02:40,328 --> 00:02:43,660
with a property that is itself an anonymous object.

38
00:02:47,860 --> 00:02:53,665
A display driver creates a strongly typed shape with Initialize and a view model class.

39
00:02:53,665 --> 00:02:58,222
This driver, from the Settings module, uses DebugSettingsViewModel.

40
00:02:58,222 --> 00:03:03,840
Without generated code, the shape is a proxy class that derives from the view model.

41
00:03:04,590 --> 00:03:09,953
The shape generator finds Initialize calls in display drivers and CreateAsync calls on

42
00:03:09,953 --> 00:03:12,693
the shape factory that name a model type.

43
00:03:12,693 --> 00:03:17,066
For each model, it writes a class that derives from it and implements

44
00:03:17,066 --> 00:03:21,030
IShape and IPositioned, and intercepts the calls to create it.

45
00:03:21,780 --> 00:03:26,644
When you own the model, mark a partial class with GenerateShape instead.

46
00:03:26,644 --> 00:03:32,131
The generator implements IShape and IPositioned on the class itself, so that model

47
00:03:32,131 --> 00:03:35,062
needs neither an interceptor nor a proxy.

48
00:03:35,062 --> 00:03:38,990
NavigationItemViewModel uses Metadata in its constructor.

49
00:03:43,190 --> 00:03:48,761
The OCSG001 analyzer reports a warning when a sealed model that does not

50
00:03:48,761 --> 00:03:55,688
implement IShape is passed to Initialize, or to a CreateAsync overload that builds a proxy.

51
00:03:55,688 --> 00:04:01,330
To fix it, remove sealed, implement IShape, or use View, Copy or Dynamic.

52
00:04:02,080 --> 00:04:05,640
The OCSG002 analyzer checks the Feature attribute.

53
00:04:05,640 --> 00:04:10,155
A marked class is used only when that feature is enabled, and the

54
00:04:10,155 --> 00:04:13,016
feature must belong to the same module.

55
00:04:13,016 --> 00:04:17,530
A name from another module is not found, so the class joins every

56
00:04:17,530 --> 00:04:19,310
feature of its module.

57
00:04:23,510 --> 00:04:28,740
In the Orchard Core solution, the shared build properties turn the generators on

58
00:04:28,740 --> 00:04:31,842
for the framework, module and theme projects.

59
00:04:31,842 --> 00:04:40,600
They reference OrchardCore.SourceGenerators as an analyzer, and add the namespace of the generated interceptors to InterceptorsNamespaces.

60
00:04:41,350 --> 00:04:46,666
A project gets generated code only when it references the generators as an analyzer.

61
00:04:46,666 --> 00:04:52,218
Without that reference, a class marked with GenerateArguments has no generated half, and

62
00:04:52,218 --> 00:04:56,470
Arguments.From falls back to reading its properties by reflection.

63
00:05:00,670 --> 00:05:06,288
Use a named class with GenerateArguments for arguments you reuse, and Arguments.From with

64
00:05:06,288 --> 00:05:09,363
an anonymous object for a value you pass once.

65
00:05:09,363 --> 00:05:14,271
Mark a view model you own with GenerateShape, and let the generator intercept

66
00:05:14,271 --> 00:05:17,110
Initialize and CreateAsync for the others.

67
00:05:19,110 --> 00:05:24,477
A named class with GenerateArguments, an anonymous object passed to Arguments.From, and a

68
00:05:24,477 --> 00:05:27,867
typed shape each move work from runtime to build time.

69
00:05:27,867 --> 00:05:33,121
The Source Generators page of the documentation covers the first two and the analyzers.

70
00:05:33,121 --> 00:05:34,590
Thanks for watching.

